39.5.m:
You sit in Ṛta;
you sit in Satya;
you sit in splendor;
you sit in luster;
you sit in glory;
you are praised;
you are a domain;
for the domain [I place] you;
for the domains [I place] you;
sit in the domains!
You are gain;
for gain may I gain you!
You are finding;
for finding may I find you!
You are work;
for work may I perform you!
You are power;
for power may I be able for you!
You are prosperity;
for prosperity may I prosper with you!
You are Gūrda;
for Gūrda [I place] you;
for the Gūrdas [I place] you;
sit in Gūrda!
Protect dominion;
make dominion swell;
quicken dominion;
uphold dominion!
You are dominion;
for dominion [I place] you;
for dominions [I place] you;
sit in dominion!
Among all earthly things I seat you;
among all atmospheric things I seat you;
among all heavenly things I seat you;
among all waters I seat you;
among all plants I seat you;
among all trees I seat you;
in all quarters I seat you;
in all intermediate quarters I seat you.
Sit in heaven!
You are winning the sun;
you are winning the battle-array;
you are winning abundance;
you are victorious;
you are all-winning;
you are winning everything;
you are winning simultaneously;
you are winning wealth;
you are shining;
you are shining out;
you are shining forth;
I seat you as the vajra that slays the rival;
I seat you as the vajra that slays the Rakṣases;
I seat you as the vajra that slays the Piśācas;
I seat you as the vajra that slays the Yātudhānas;
I seat you as the vajra that slays the niggards;
I seat you as the vajra that slays the adversaries;
you are slayer of the foe; I seat you as the Indra-vajra that slays the foe, slays the rival, slays the Asuras!

39.6.m:
You are ascending;
you are rising;
you are mounting;
you are stepping forward;
you are stepping upon;
you are conquest;
you are stepping together;
you are crossing over;
you are transition;
you are heavenly;
you are heaven.
Sit in refreshment!
Sit in nourishment!
Sit in good fortune!
Sit in wealth!
Sit in prosperity!
Sit on the sacrificial [spot] of the earth!
Sit in the step of Viṣṇu!
Sit in the step of Iḍā!
Sit in the ghee-holding!
Sit in the overflowing!
Sit in the year (Saṃvatsara)!
Sit in the Parivatsara!
Sit in the Idāvatsara!
Sit in the Anuvatsara!
Sit in the Udvatsara!
Sit in the one!
Sit in the ten!
Sit in the hundred!
Sit in the thousand!
Sit in the ten thousand!
Sit in the hundred thousand!
Sit in the million!
Sit in the hundred million (arbuda)!
Sit in the thousand million (nyarbuda)!
Sit in the badva!
Sit in the ocean (samudra)!
Sit in the middle!
Sit at the end!
Sit in the highest number (parārdha)!
You are overflowing;
for the overflowing one [I place] you;
for the overflowing ones [I place] you;
sit in the overflowing!
You are Ṛta;
for Ṛta [I place] you;
for the Ṛtas [I place] you;
sit in Ṛta!
You are Satya;
for Satya [I place] you;
for the Satyas [I place] you;
sit in Satya!
You are the joint;
for the joint [I place] you;
for the joints [I place] you;
sit in the joints!
You are the union;
for the union [I place] you;
for the unions [I place] you;
sit in the unions!
You are fulfillment;
for fulfillment [I place] you;
for fulfillments [I place] you;
sit in fulfillments!

39.7.m:
The eastern quarter;
the Gāyatrī meter;
the Rathantara Sāman;
Agni the deity;
spring the season;
the Trivṛt Stoma with the fifteenfold course;
age of three years the strength;
the Kṛta among the throws of dice;
the east wind the wind;
Sānaga the ṛṣi.
The southern quarter;
the Triṣṭubh meter;
the Bṛhat Sāman;
Indra the deity;
summer the season;
the Pañcadaśa Stoma with the seventeenfold course;
a two-and-a-half-year-old steer the strength;
the Tretā among the throws of dice;
the south wind the wind;
Pratna the ṛṣi.
The western quarter;
the Jagatī meter;
the Vairūpa Sāman;
the Maruts the deity;
the rains the season;
the Saptadaśa Stoma with the twenty-onefold course;
a three-year-old steer the strength;
the Dvāpara among the throws of dice;
the west wind the wind;
Sanātana the ṛṣi.
The northern quarter;
the Anuṣṭubh meter;
the Vairāja Sāman;
the Viśve Devas the deity;
autumn the season;
the Ekaviṃśa Stoma with the twenty-sevenfold course;
a four-year-old steer the strength;
the Āskanda among the throws of dice;
the north wind the wind;
Purāṇa the ṛṣi.
The upward quarter;
the Paṅkti meter;
the Śākvara and Raivata Sāmans;
Mitra and Varuṇa the deity;
winter and cool season the seasons;
the Triṇava Stoma with the thirty-threefold course;
a five-year-old ox the strength;
the Abhibhū among the throws of dice;
the wind from all directions the wind;
Suparṇa the ṛṣi.
Fathers, grandfathers, from higher to lower, may they protect us, may they help us,
in this Brahman, in this dominion, in this blessing, in this priestly office, in this invocation of the gods!
By that Brahman, by that meter, by that deity, like an Aṅgiras, sit firm!

39.8.m:
Extend out in breath from life;
extend out through-breath from out-breath;
extend out in-breath from through-breath;
extend out sight from in-breath;
extend out hearing from sight;
extend out speech from hearing;
extend out the self from speech;
extend out the earth from the self;
extend out the intermediate space from the earth;
extend out heaven from the intermediate space;
extend out the sun from heaven.
The earth is the barren cow, the new moon the embryo, the plants the afterbirth, Agni the calf, the Agnihotra the colostrum.
The intermediate space is the barren cow, Dhātṛ the embryo, the Rudras the afterbirth, Vāyu the calf, the Gharma the colostrum.
Heaven is the barren cow, thunder the embryo, the constellations the afterbirth, Sūrya the calf, rain the colostrum.
The Ṛgveda is the barren cow, the Bṛhat and Rathantara the embryo, the summons and Nivids the afterbirth, the sacrifice the calf, the sacrificial fee the colostrum.
The commoners are the barren cow, the warrior is the embryo, the cattle are the afterbirth, the king is the calf, tribute is the colostrum.

39.9.m:
You are the maker of increase;
you are the maker of wide space;
you face east;
you face upward;
you are the intermediate space.
Giver of splendor, I set you in splendor;
giver of luster, I set you in luster;
giver of milk, I set you in milk;
giver of fame, I set you in fame;
giver of wealth, I set you in wealth;
I set you in the wealth of the earth;
I set you in the wealth of the intermediate space;
I set you in the wealth of heaven;
I set you in the wealth of the quarters;
giver of wealth, I set you in wealth.
You sit in the waters;
you sit in the birds;
you sit in the falcon;
you sit in the vulture;
you sit in the eagle.
The goddess who you are, O brick, giving life, lying close beside [us],
lie close beside me, just as a wife [lies] ever beside her husband.
The goddess who you are, O brick, giving out-breath, giving through-breath, giving in-breath, giving sight, giving hearing, giving speech, giving the self, giving earth, giving intermediate space, giving heaven, giving the sun, giving maidens, giving wanton girls, giving women with their first head-ornament, giving young women, lying close beside [us],
lie close beside me, just as a wife [lies] ever beside her husband.

39.10.m:
This indeed is she who shone forth first; entering into these she moves within.
The bride, the newly-calved mother, has lowed; three greatnesses attend upon her.
Possessing meters, the two dawns, adorned, move together along the common womb;
the two wives of the sun wander knowing, bearing signs, unaging, rich in seed.
Three have arrived following the path of Ṛta; three Gharmas have arrived following seed.
One protects the offspring, one the nourishment, one protects the dominion of the god-seeking.
She who was fourth established the four-stoma sacrifice, becoming the wings of the sacrifice, the ṛṣis;
Gāyatrī, Triṣṭubh, Jagatī, Virāj, yoking the solar chant, brought hither this sun.
When Dhātṛ arranged this [world] with five, he generated sisters for them, five by five;
and of them five go forth in succession, the intentions putting on various forms.
Along the five dawnings are the five milkings, the seasons five along the five-named cow;
the five quarters arranged by the fifteenfold [stoma], having a common summit toward one world.
Luminous, goddess Dawn puts on the cloud, according to the ordinance of Sūrya;
the cattle, being born manifold in form, look out from the lap of this mother.
Thirty sisters approach the appointed rendezvous, putting on a common sign;
the wise extend the seasons, knowing them; luminous, they go around in the midst of the meters.
With a bright bull, with cloud, with light she has come, all-formed, variegated, with the beacon of fire;
doing good work toward a common goal, bringing old age, you, unaging Dawn, have arrived.
The mistress of the seasons, this first one has arrived, leader of days, mother of offspring;
being one, O Dawn, shine forth manifold; unaged yourself, make everything else grow old.
First dawning at the domain of Ṛta, one bears the greatness of the waters;
one moves at the appointed places of Sūrya, one of the Gharma, one does Savitṛ hold fast.
The Ekāṣṭakā, practicing ascetic heat, brought forth the embryo, the greatness, Indra;
by him the gods overcame the Dasyus; by his powers he became the slayer of the Asuras.
‘You have made me younger who had no younger sister,’ speaking truth, follow this [demand];
may I be in his favor as you [are]; let not one of you drive past another!
Now the all-knowing one has been in our favor; he has reached a firm foundation, they have found a ford;
may I be in his favor as you [are]; let not one of you drive past another!
First she shone forth; she became a milch cow with Yama;
rich in milk, may she milk for us year after year!

39.11.m:
With Agni, overcoming through Ṛta;
with intention, the lord of power;
with goodwill, heavenly;
with sacrifice, the generous one;
with fury, the slayer of Vṛtra;
with the bull, Tvaṣṭṛ;
with the Vaṣaṭ call, partaking of the half;
of the earth, the grass-blade;
with food, Gaya;
with the Sāman, possessed of a body;
with the Ṛg verses, eating food;
with ascetic heat, unassailable;
with the sun, sovereign ruler;
with the seasons he flourished;
with the year he encompassed all.
Both prevailing and to be prevailed over;
both advancing in strength and of high strength;
both of equal strength and of great strength;
both victorious and more powerful;
both overpowering and mighty.
Unto you, O hero, we shout praises;
for you alone do we invoke.

40.1.m:
Hiraṇyagarbha arose in the beginning; born, he was the sole lord of what has come into being.
He sustained this earth and heaven: to which god shall we make offering with the oblation?
Who became king of what breathes and winks, the sole lord of the whole world;
who rules over this two-footed and four-footed: to which god shall we make offering with the oblation?
Who is the giver of spirit, the giver of strength; whose command all, whose command the gods attend;
whose shadow is immortality, whose shadow is death: to which god shall we make offering with the oblation?
By whom the mighty heaven and the earth were made firm, by whom the sun was propped up, by whom the firmament;
who measured out the wide midspace: to which god shall we make offering with the oblation?
Who supported these two, heaven and earth, propped up though trembling;
upon whom the sun, extended, travels: to which god shall we make offering with the oblation?
Whose are all these mountains by his greatness; whose, they say, is the ocean together with the Rasā;
whose regions are the five divine directions: to which god shall we make offering with the oblation?
When the great waters came over all, holding the embryo and generating Agni,
thence arose the one life-spirit of the gods: to which god shall we make offering with the oblation?
May Prajāpati generate offspring for us; may the Creator, benevolent, ordain [it];
and the Year, in harmony with the seasons; may the lord of nourishment bestow nourishment upon me.

40.2.m:
With out-breath and in-breath as my yoked pair, I yoke you.
With the two butter-pourings as my yoked pair, I yoke you.
With Indra and Agni as my yoked pair, I yoke you.
With the meters, you;
with the stomas, you;
with the ukthas, you;
for fiery energy, you;
for splendor, you;
for wealth, you;
for nourishment, you; for leadership among my kinsmen, with me as your yoked pair, I yoke you.
O Agni, as a bull generating [you] again young, attentive, I have approached you.
May our household rites not run on one bull; sharpen us together with sharp sacred formula!
Those who attend on you, O Night, as the likeness of the year,
unite their long-lived offspring with wealth and nourishment!

40.4.m:
I seat you upon the red clouds.
I seat you upon the ruddy clouds.
I seat you upon the black, upon the dark-blue, upon the dark clouds.
Ambā is your name;
Dulā is your name;
Nitatnī is your name;
Cupuṇīkā is your name;
Abhrayantī is your name;
Meghayantī is your name;
Varṣayantī is your name.
I seat you full of light.
I seat you light-maker.
I seat you light-finding.
I seat you blazing.
I seat you shining.
I seat you glimmering.
I seat you radiant.
I seat you of great light.
I seat you bright.
I seat you waking [others].
I seat you wakeful.
I seat you unceasing.
For impulsion, you;
for support, you;
for side-glance, you;
for the surging wave, you;
for the stream, you;
for the ocean, you;
for the lake, you;
for all-encompassing space, you;
for the supporter, you;
for wealth, you;
for good fortune, you;
for the intermediate space, you!

40.6.m:
Father Mātariśvan has set down unbroken foot-tracks;
the unbroken Uśijas, the inspired sages, carved the tracks;
Soma the all-knower, the leader, will lead;
Bṛhaspati will recite the hymns of joy.
When you cried out…
Given by Yama, Trita yoked him; Indra first mounted him;
the Gandharva seized his rein; from the sun the Vasus fashioned the horse.
You are Yama, you are Āditya, O courser; you are Trita by secret ordinance;
you are thoroughly united with Soma; they say you have three bonds in heaven.
They say you have three bonds in heaven, three in the waters, three within the sea;
and to me you seem like Varuṇa, O courser, where they say is your highest birthplace.
These are your groomings, O prize-runner, these the placings of the hooves of Savitṛ;
here I have seized your auspicious testicles, which the guardians of truth watch over.
You are the Saṃvatsara;
you are the Parivatsara;
you are the Idāvatsara;
you are the Anuvatsara;
you are the Udvatsara.
At the impulsion of divine Savitṛ, with the arms of the Aśvins, with the hands of Pūṣan, I seat you accompanied by Indra.
You are the cloak of the domain;
sit in your own womb, sit in your own womb of earth!
May the seasons be arranged for you!
May the months be arranged for you!
May the half-months be arranged for you!
May the days and nights be arranged for you!
May the limbs be arranged for you!
May the joints be arranged for you!
May the bodies be arranged for you!
Coming and going, bend together and stretch out!
Agni is light, light is Agni;
Indra is light, light is Indra;
the Sun is light, light is the Sun.
Suck this nourishing, swollen breast of the waters, O Agni, in the midst of the watery flood;
enjoy the spring, the honeyed wave; enter the ocean dwelling!

40.7.m:
From the ocean the honeyed wave has arisen; together with the Upāṃśu cup it has attained immortality,
which is the secret name of ghee, the tongue of the gods, the navel of immortality.
Let us proclaim the name of ghee; in this sacrifice let us uphold it with homages;
may the Brahman priest listen to it being praised; the four-horned buffalo has bellowed this forth.
Four are his horns, three are his feet, two are his heads, seven are his hands;
bound in three ways, the bull bellows aloud; the great god has entered into mortals.
Placed in three ways, hidden by the Paṇis, the gods found the ghee within the cow;
Indra generated one, the Sun one; from Vena they carved out one through inherent power.
These flow from the ocean of the heart, having a hundred enclosures, not to be looked upon by the enemy;
I behold the streams of ghee; in their midst is a golden reed.
They flow together like rivers, like streams of milk, being purified inwardly with heart and mind;
these waves of ghee rush onward like deer fleeing from an archer.
Like swift ones on the course of a river, breaking wind, the young waters fly;
the streams of ghee swell with waves like a reddish prize-horse bursting through the course.
They stream forward toward Agni like lovely women smiling on their way to a festival;
the streams of ghee reach the kindling-logs; enjoying them, Jātavedas is pleased.
I look upon them as upon maidens anointing themselves with anointment to go to a bridal procession;
where the soma is pressed, where the sacrifice is, thither flow the streams of ghee.
Flow toward the praise-song, toward the contest for cattle; bestow auspicious riches upon us;
lead this sacrifice of ours to the gods; the streams of ghee flow sweet with honey.
Upon your seat the whole world is rested, within the ocean, within the heart, within life;
that honeyed wave of yours which was brought in the assembly, at the battle-line of waters—may we obtain that!
